      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Behavior\n\n## Implemented behavior\n\n`resolveContentPayload` normalizes the payload; `resolveViewContent` finds delegated material. ContentNode and ViewContentPayload render the supported material through the existing payload renderers. A View may instead own its own data.content.\n\n## Known gaps\n\nThe previous plan listed only six kinds; the payload normalizer also recognizes canvas. This spec documents all seven without promoting canvas rendering into a new semantic primitive. Browser rendering and external image delivery are separate from payload normalization tests.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNo additional decision is required to describe the behavior above. Changes to that contract require an explicit task; implementation gaps are not implied approvals.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource (twilite repository):\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/contentPayload.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/Nodes/ContentNode.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/Nodes/ViewNode.js`\n\nFocused tests (twilite repository):\n- `tests/contentPayload.test.js`\n- `tests/viewOwnContentPortal.test.js`\n\nThese pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.\n\nRenderer boundary: The content normalizer and inline preview mapper recognize canvas, but ContentNode and ViewContentPayload currently use a fallback textual preview rather than a dedicated canvas renderer. Accepting a payload kind in the normalizer does not prove every View host has a dedicated renderer for it."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-content",
          "nodeId": "content-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "content-representations",
      "label": "Representations",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": 120,
        "y": 1040
      },
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 660,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Representations\n\nOne Content value can have several Views. Material kind selects a payload renderer; Surface and View selection choose the presentation. A selected representation uses the existing workspace frame. Surface, resolution and focus changes do not implicitly resize it, reflow neighbors or change camera zoom. Manual resizing is explicit. Internal nodes, edges, handles and pointer targets are clipped; exposed boundary controls remain accessible. Workspace title bars belong to View representations (including glyph-shaped artwork), not a terminal Glyph."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-content",
          "nodeId": "content-representations"
        }
      }
    },
